 Canaan (16:3; 21:5).","verses":18,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Hagar","v":[11,15,16]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[3]},{"id":"shur_1090","name":"Shur","kind":"","lat":30.2354,"lon":33.247,"summary":"An enclosure; a wall, a part, probably, of the Arabian desert, on the north-eastern border of Egypt, giving its name to a wilderness extending from Egypt toward Philistia (Gen. 16:7; 20:1; 25:18; Ex. 15:22).","verses":6,"v":[7]},{"id":"bered_178","name":"Bered","kind":"City","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"A town in the south of Palestine (Gen. 16:14), in the desert of Shur, near Lahai-roi.","verses":1,"v":[14]},{"id":"kadesh_661","name":"Kadesh","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":15,"v":[14]}],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_ishmael_76","title":"Birth of Ishmael","year":-1910,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 16:11–16. People: Ishmael, Abraham, Hagar.","v":[11,12,13,14,15,16]},{"id":"lifetime_of_ishmael_77","title":"Lifetime of Ishmael","year":-1910,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 16:16–25:17. People: Ishmael. Lasted about 137 years.","v":[16]}],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[87,87,802,8297,3205,3205,0,3808,3808,0,4713,4713,4713,4713,8198,8034,1904],[8297,8297,559,413,87,2009,4994,3068,3068,6113,6113,6113,3205,3205,3205,4994,935,413,8198,8198,194,1129,1129,1129,1129,1129,4480,4480,87,87,8085,6963,6963,6963,8297,8297],[7093,7093,87,3427,3427,3667,3667,6235,6235,8141,87,802,8297,3947,4713,4713,8198,1904,5414,5